<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:51Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Police make seventh arrest over UK airbase incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fe897b333372b65f7faac137b1b9b49d2891d6e305d624d9adc9221ac51f893</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:51:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident--a2cfc3b816d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident" /><summary type="html">A seventh man was arrested Tuesday over a major incident last month at a British military airbase used by the United States to launch strikes on Iran, police said. The arrest came a day after President Donald Trump said the United States had withdrawn all B-1 bombers from RAF Fairford because of "threats" he believed were linked to Tehran. A 22-year-old British male was arrested in London "on suspicion of preparation of terrorist acts", Britain's Counter-Terrorism Policing network said in a statement. Six men in their 20s have already been arrested and released on bail after three suspicious vans were stopped near the base in southwest England on September 27. FRANCE 24's Bénédicte Paviot reports from London.</summary></entry><entry><title>German ex-spy chief arrested for suspected espionage, treason</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51cd46b7f870efa0e033ac4ee6573d7d6dec240023020877c4605fbd51a0abfe</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:42:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason--cbca89fe2a12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason" /><summary type="html">A former German spy chief was arrested Tuesday on suspicion of espionage and treason, an embarrassing case at a time when the country is seeking to broaden the powers of its intelligence agencies. August Hanning, who ran Germany's BND foreign intelligence agency from 1998 to 2005, is accused of espionage, treason and working for foreign intelligence services, federal prosecutors said. FRANCE 24's Nick Holdsworth reports from Berlin.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Busification': Inside Ukraine’s controversial recruitment practices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e4fdd6f71dd86c5c30893f6da40f29ae8a30e41028bf161060453b6ae7bee75</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:19:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-busification-inside-ukraine-s-controversial-recruitment-practices--28bf4e6cdcb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-busification-inside-ukraine-s-controversial-recruitment-practices" /><summary type="html">Recent reports and videos of alleged recruitment irregularities are fuelling tensions between mobilisation authorities and Ukrainian society, while raising questions about the oversight and implementation of military recruitment.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK police arrest 22-year-old British man in suspected Fairford base plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db165f480915dfdf7b424289e60659463bfb02bddd0e4497b9631916d46ef09f</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:26:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-uk-police-make-new-arrest-in-suspected-air-base-plot--cc7e5c5471a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-uk-police-make-new-arrest-in-suspected-air-base-plot" /><summary type="html">UK ​police on Tuesday said they had ​arrested ‌a ⁠22-year ‌old British man ⁠in London on suspicion ​of preparing terrorist acts ‌in relation ​to the suspected plot at the ​RAF ​Fairford ​airbase used ​by the US to strike Iran.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Catalan separatist Puigdemont cleared to return to Spain after court lifts arrest warrant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1655198dcba6b2b021be973a6ad8431bb3558d99d9d218822b99eea15d42fafd</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:10:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-exiled-catalan-separatist-leader-puigdemont-cleared-to-return-to-spain--8ba16e2f1ed9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-exiled-catalan-separatist-leader-puigdemont-cleared-to-return-to-spain" /><summary type="html">A Spanish Supreme Court judge on Tuesday lifted the arrest warrant for Catalan separatist leader Carles Puigdemont, clearing the way for him to return home without fear of detention ahead of a general election in November.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Should we be worried about a plague outbreak in Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3db76db2abc123b334286f3088ab3697288e57a4351fdcc38dece50ba24caad7</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:30:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261006-should-we-be-worried-about-a-plague-outbreak-in-russia--38fad56138a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261006-should-we-be-worried-about-a-plague-outbreak-in-russia" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, October 6: The death of a researcher in Siberia, reportedly from the plague, sparks concern despite Russian authorities' denial. But first: French high school protesters are promising "Act 3" of their protest movement against learning conditions. Also, Le Monde speaks to the editor of Russian independent outlet Novaya Gazeta ahead of the 20th anniversary of the murder of investigative journalist Anna Politkovskaya. Finally, it appears that butter is back in fashion.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria searches for missing crew as drones hit two Black Sea ships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2d60ec95dbe6fe4a6fc435febb3fc49b98bf0853b291e95a3299574c5187fbb</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:24:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-bulgaria-searches-for-missing-crew-as-drones-hit-two-more-black-sea-ships--a9c664076180.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-bulgaria-searches-for-missing-crew-as-drones-hit-two-more-black-sea-ships" /><summary type="html">Bulgarian authorities on Tuesday launched a search for missing crew members of a boat that sank in its economic zone in the Black Sea after drones hit two merchant vessels. Black Sea shipping has been hit by growing fallout from the war in Ukraine in recent months.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine hits Moscow with one of its largest drone attacks in two years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:644defbddc21bd67af4bb300d04c31e29def769736dffaf35b7cc88ab8d5c982</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T06:11:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-massive-ukrainian-drone-attack-targets-moscow-russian-officials-say--d7ae0a7240b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-massive-ukrainian-drone-attack-targets-moscow-russian-officials-say" /><summary type="html">Ukraine launched overnight one of its largest drone attacks on Moscow in the past two years, killing two men and injuring several people in the Russian capital, local officials said on Tuesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Live: French interior ministry estimates 250,000 join student protests, organisers claim 450,000</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24e371bd51036b40d747067476575a9c0d0d01e3a7848e17c8a0f4d061f6c81c</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T02:31:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students--df93e10e4e3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students" /><summary type="html">Around 250,000 people joined student protests across France on Tuesday, according to the French interior ministry. Organisers of the mass demonstrations put the figure of 450,000. Clashes erupted in some cities between the police and demonstrators demanding more education funding and resources on the biggest day yet of student protests. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds arrested on biggest day of French student protests over education resources</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b84957c0b10bcf98619c4210f15ffb1007dfd38346db6b64d83c48fda5b9dad3</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T02:06:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-gen-z-has-risen-up-tens-of-thousands-demand-better-education-in-france--ed0f874f63fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-gen-z-has-risen-up-tens-of-thousands-demand-better-education-in-france" /><summary type="html">Mass protests over decrepit conditions at France's high schools descended into sporadic violence Tuesday, leading to nearly 500 arrests and prompting President Emmanuel Macron to call an emergency meeting. Members of the public have accused the authorities of using disproportionate force as protesters clashed with the police in several French cities.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Sanchez chose 'best moment in a sea of troubles' to call for snap election, analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8df44378853ad7c51263817fd0d8d70e545c445887c8aa39ba67a7fceb5a597</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T19:31:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sanchez-chose-best-moment-in-a-sea-of-troubles-to-call-for-snap-election-analyst-says--d3b32568f53b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sanchez-chose-best-moment-in-a-sea-of-troubles-to-call-for-snap-election-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Monday called an early election for November 29, aiming to increase his parliamentary support after lawmakers last week rejected proposals to address a housing crisis that has drawn nationwide protests. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Javier Carbonell, Policy Analyst at the European Policy Centre, explains that Sanchez has chosen "the best moment in a sea of troubles" to call snap elections as he is likely to capitalise on the mobilisation of left-wing voters during the housing protests.</summary></entry><entry><title>France, Germany seek new EU rapid response tool against trade threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16b4ec3a125bff93a5b668ed7fce17e4a66fce169c1016f3154ea6a68f599e8b</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:01:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-france-germany-seek-new-eu-rapid-response-tool-against-trade-threats--a4fdd4599ffc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-france-germany-seek-new-eu-rapid-response-tool-against-trade-threats" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and German Chancellor Friedrich Merz on Monday announced they would develop a new legal tool to enable the EU to respond rapidly to trade wars or measures, such as dumping. While they did not say the proposal was a direct response to the actions of any particular country, it came days before EU Chief Ursula von der Leyen visits China to tackle trade frictions.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>ISIS suspects face 'outsourced' justice in Iraq as HRW warns of 'collective global detention crisis'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d00f36db3d5d968716c7255345b076e4cb40fadc3b735f98b3b460dd81201aad</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:46:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-c--177d80f183d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-crisis-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Letta Tayler, Senior Counterterrorism Advisor at Human Rights Watch. She warns of the detention of suspected Islamic State members transferred from northeast Syria to Iraq as part of a much wider "global detention crisis". The men and boys now held in Iraq are living in 'dire' conditions, including deaths from illness, allegations of torture, and serious questions surrounding access to effective legal representation. Can accountability be achieved through legal proceedings that respect the rule of law and provide genuine justice to both detainees and victims?</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron slams Russia’s ‘irresponsible’ strikes on Ukraine’s civilian infrastructure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb732b16915c339ccf2b3f8954fbcbecb30f025805523e829f881da2170a14b3</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:09:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-macron-slams-russia-s-irresponsible-strikes-on-ukraine-s-civilian-infrastructure--b2598d84b925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-macron-slams-russia-s-irresponsible-strikes-on-ukraine-s-civilian-infrastructure" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Monday slammed Russia's increased strikes on Ukrainian civilian infrastructure. In a phone call with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, Macron said he reviewed "the concrete support" Europe can provide Ukraine to defend itself against the attacks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: 'Mini-hurricane' kills at least two people in Catalonia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61b9def11fb2401e9bd50da4263c46c3ff91837f58fbc0df39f3fa8e9230534e</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T13:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-spain-mini-hurricane-kills-at-least-two-people-in-catalonia--003d1b82f1f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-spain-mini-hurricane-kills-at-least-two-people-in-catalonia" /><summary type="html">Two people have ⁠died and ​another is missing after heavy rains and flooding in Spain's ​Catalonia region, authorities said on Sunday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ex-prince Andrew launches bid to ‘quash’ Epstein-affair search warrants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ca0da96c75a2bec5dd3d18ec809d969597488de0f815f762a15172889412c91</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T08:36:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-ex-prince-andrew-launches-bid-to-quash-epstein-affair-search-warrants--49712c346881.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-ex-prince-andrew-launches-bid-to-quash-epstein-affair-search-warrants" /><summary type="html">Britain's disgraced former prince, Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor, filed a legal action on Monday to quash warrants that led to searches of his residences. The police arrested the 66-year-old on February 19 on suspicion of misconduct over his links to the late convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish PM Sanchez calls snap election as pressure mounts over housing crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e83dc32d0dae27871f3944c954435f7cf1847f618aac8b81528154bec757aee</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T07:18:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-spanish-pm-sanchez-calls-snap-election-for-november-29--03dd8b408d88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-spanish-pm-sanchez-calls-snap-election-for-november-29" /><summary type="html">Spanish ​Prime ​Minister ​Pedro Sanchez on Monday called an early ​election ‌for ‌November ​29. Facing the electorate now could be risky, as Sanchez's Socialist Party is trailing in opinion polls.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio visits Iceland ‘to discuss security collaboration’ as US boosts Arctic presence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35d210fa9cfa2e0a8524896417057e08b4ff853c2d0a9f5fc092e61d164d8e2d</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T01:20:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-rubio-visits-iceland-as-us-boosts-arctic-presence-after-greenland-security-pact--fbd4e46a038b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-rubio-visits-iceland-as-us-boosts-arctic-presence-after-greenland-security-pact" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is set to travel to Iceland on Monday, two weeks after Washington sealed a security pact with Denmark and Greenland on the sidelines of the United Nations General Assembly. Rubio will meet with officials in Reykjavik "to discuss economic and security collaboration", according to a statement by the US State Department.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US withdraws B-1 bombers from British military base RAF Fairford amid security concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44f622d8b88c9196b31c51bde4b1ae579307107ca19d1d358fbe8d706e1d0a70</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T22:50:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-us-bombers-raf-fairford-uk-pentagon--df59450487f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-us-bombers-raf-fairford-uk-pentagon" /><summary type="html">The Pentagon confirmed on Sunday that all US B-1 bombers deployed to Britain’s RAF Fairford had returned home following a security incident that prompted nearby evacuations. Police found no explosives after reports of suspicious activity at the base last Sunday. Five London-based British men arrested were subsequently released on bail.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Tsar Samuel laid to rest in Sofia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b7ec778ccebf29f6e2881a64ce291bb4ab74517f00d96dcc2b8ac3774f1176d</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T08:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tsar-samuel-laid-to-rest-in-sofia--83ea100649cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tsar-samuel-laid-to-rest-in-sofia" /><summary type="html">In Bulgaria, the remains of medieval ruler Tsar Samuel have been laid to rest in the capital Sofia, after being flown back from the border with Greece by Bulgarian fighter jets. Their return follows decades of negotiations with Athens, in exchange for the return of religious artefacts. Nicholas Rushworth has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Merz unveils new aid for Ukraine as Russia strikes Kyiv during German leader's visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f15514de9caae3990dae940bc2ac9de1d9babb65ba8602c3a986329c07617abe</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T08:38:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-merz-unveils-new-aid-for-ukraine-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-during-german-leader-s-visit--40cc8c9523ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-merz-unveils-new-aid-for-ukraine-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-during-german-leader-s-visit" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz announced a new aid package for Ukraine worth more than 1.3 billion euros ($1.5 billion) during a visit to Kyiv on Sunday marked by renewed Russian attacks on the Ukrainian capital, including the latest drone attack on a bridge spanning the Dnipro River.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz visits Kyiv as Russia steps up attacks on Ukrainian cities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:befc6761136e42e750b7e3e4c85a53ac8cc343eb2101637229141ea9270f8ddb</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T07:58:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/germany-s-merz-visits-kyiv-as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-cities--909b7f6cda4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-s-merz-visits-kyiv-as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-cities" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz arrived in Ukraine's capital Kyiv on Sunday on an unannounced visit in a show of support for the country in its war with Russia. Merz's visit comes just a day after Russia warned foreigners and diplomats to leave the Ukrainian capital, saying that "massive" new airstrikes would hit the city. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv Gulliver Cragg has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US wants to hold trilateral Ukraine talks with Russia by end of October, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97f80609f5ee813e74b72106d2980268bd5d8858bc6ae22e1d53f445372e29e8</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T07:28:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-live-germany-s-merz-in-kyiv-for-talks-with-zelensky--c94ea41cc266.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-live-germany-s-merz-in-kyiv-for-talks-with-zelensky" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Sunday that the US wants to broker a new round of talks with Ukraine and Russia on ending the war and hold it by the end of October. Earlier, Kyiv Mayor Vitali Klitschko said the city's Northern Bridge over the Dnipro River was again hit in a Russian attack during a visit by German Chancellor Friedrich Merz. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia votes in general election with wartime divisions still dominating</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19f3485391644b6d65a4c63808d2780ad7f2ebb481f4a4aef9510c42ff9f58f1</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T06:51:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bosnia-votes-in-general-election-with-wartime-divisions-still-dominating--9c5edfbb2a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bosnia-votes-in-general-election-with-wartime-divisions-still-dominating" /><summary type="html">Bosnia is heading to the polls on Sunday after a general election campaign dominated by parties that identify closely with the ethnic divisions of its 1990s war. Voters will elect a vast number of officials across multiple tiers of government, in a complex system that has held the partitioned country together since the 1995 peace deal. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Belgrade Laurent Rouy has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bosnians vote as pro-Russian politician looms large and ethnic tensions simmer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dccba077c85a32477bc3b72627b333393f62193d7ed018de1daaed0d6616c431</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T05:55:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-polls-open-in-bosnia-and-herzegovina-as-pro-russian-politician-looms-large-over-race--bba810cbe218.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-polls-open-in-bosnia-and-herzegovina-as-pro-russian-politician-looms-large-over-race" /><summary type="html">Bosnians head to the polls Sunday in elections that ​could impact how much influence Russia has over the small Balkan nation, with separatist Serb leader Milorad Dodik dominating the campaign despite his ban from public office. Bosnia and Herzegovina, a country marred by ethnic tensions, has struggled to recover since its brutal 1992-95 conflict.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Latvia's PM on track to lead pro-Ukraine coalition after parliamentary election victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdd0fa7d3510a8a33c1c77a618b777c86112ec7dda70abf4034dbfce61d23446</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T20:58:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-latvia-elections-pm-kulbergs-pro-ukraine-party-ahead-coalition-partners-stumble--25ca306cac3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-latvia-elections-pm-kulbergs-pro-ukraine-party-ahead-coalition-partners-stumble" /><summary type="html">Latvian ​Prime Minister Andris Kulbergs was set to retain power and form a coalition after his centrist United List won parliamentary elections on Sunday, the biggest in the country's post-independence history. While the result is expected to reinforce the Baltic country’s pro-European and pro-Ukrainian stance, populist parties also made significant gains.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Putin's war for the history books: Dmytro Kuleba speaks to FRANCE 24</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:473f7b3bec16fba2041a3e53ee49e81f94b2be23a44a35667af34e9a68ecc81a</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T18:08:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261003-putin-s-war-for-the-history-books-dmytro-kuleba-speaks-to-france-24--8a38a0a2beb7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261003-putin-s-war-for-the-history-books-dmytro-kuleba-speaks-to-france-24" /><summary type="html">The Bronze Horseman, the iconic equestrian statue in Senate Square in St Petersburg, was commissioned by Catherine the Great in honor of Peter the Great, the city's founder. The pedestal of the statue bears a laconic dedication: "To Peter the First, Catherine the Second, 1782". Does Putin want to be the third, Vladimir the Great? And is that ambition – expansion at any cost – the real reason behind the war in Ukraine? According to former Ukrainian foreign minister Dmytro Kuleba, "Putin only cares about what will be written about him in history books."</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Italy’s Ustica enigma: Can French files solve mystery crash blamed on stray missile?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7322dc1f068556b90045bc9728d0d660c6ea078e19d304eefc2e2392850f2992</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T15:42:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-italy-ustica-enigma-can-french-files-solve-mystery-crash-blamed-on-stray-missile-gaddafi--dd128b356206.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-italy-ustica-enigma-can-french-files-solve-mystery-crash-blamed-on-stray-missile-gaddafi" /><summary type="html">France’s decision to share defence documents with the Italian judiciary has raised hopes of a breakthrough in investigations into the 1980 crash of a passenger jet near the island of Ustica, which a former Italian president claimed was mistakenly shot down by a French fighter jet. Sceptics caution that the files are unlikely to shed light on one of Italy’s most enduring mysteries, let alone reveal a culprit.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Fresh protests over housing flare in Spain after lawmakers reject relief measures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc89d4459f2ca8cd0012e75729b31b282d16a27bdb255874de985c4da412d027</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T13:20:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-fresh-protests-over-housing-flare-spain-after-lawmakers-reject-relief-measures--704e7b8d4986.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-fresh-protests-over-housing-flare-spain-after-lawmakers-reject-relief-measures" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of protesters marched in Madrid and other cities in Spain on Saturday to demand affordable housing, fuelled by anger at lawmakers who narrowly rejected measures put forward by the government of Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez to strengthen protection for tenants.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes another Kyiv bridge, deepening travel chaos in Ukraine's capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e70e0fc019afcbac1ad28d7dddc7790397f371d5657cdae577743f547afba30c</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:40:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-russia-strikes-another-major-bridge-in-kyiv--263369bf48e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-russia-strikes-another-major-bridge-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Kyiv's Northern Bridge across the Dnipro river was hit by a Russian air attack, Mayor Vitali Klitschko said Saturday, deepening travel chaos amid an escalation in strikes ​on ‌infrastructure in the Ukrainian capital. The latest attack comes a day after the city's Southern Bridge was hit by several strikes that officials said were "tearing Kyiv apart".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
